# .gitignore for clouddbRemapPlayer
#
# Simpler than the other three trees (clouddbGoLauncher/clouddbSEA/clouddbGo)
# — no embedded payload, no build-output folders to worry about. Just the
# standard Go pattern plus this tool's own test artifacts.

# Build output
/clouddb-remap-player.exe
*.exe

# go.sum is intentionally NOT ignored — track it once `go mod tidy` (see
# BUILD.md step 2) generates it, same reasoning as any other Go module:
# reproducible builds depend on the exact resolved dependency checksums
# being committed, not regenerated fresh by whoever clones this later.

# Test artifacts from BUILD.md's step 4 (testing against a copy, never the
# live database) — never commit a real or test SQLite file, and never
# commit the tool's own automatic backups.
test-cloudstorage.db
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.bak
